{% comment %}
  Product hero gallery — the shared presentation for the storefront's product
  page: an edge-to-edge looping image gallery, a product information panel and
  a sticky purchase bar that docks at the end of the section.

  Rendered by sections/product-hero-gallery.liquid, and by
  sections/main-product.liquid when its Hero gallery layout is switched on, so
  the two can never drift apart.

  Must be rendered inside a <product-info> element, which is the caller's — it
  is what the theme's variant swap, cart and checkout behaviour hangs off, and
  it carries the section padding and colour scheme.

  Accepts (all optional except product):
  - product: {Object} the product to render.
  - slides_desktop / slides_tablet / slides_mobile: {Number} images per view.
  - gallery_ratio: {String} aspect-ratio for every slide, e.g. '4 / 5'.
  - gallery_max_height: {Number} share of viewport height the gallery may take.
  - slide_gap: {Number} px between slides.
  - full_bleed: {Boolean} break the gallery out to the viewport width.
  - autoplay / autoplay_speed / transition_speed: {Boolean|Number} carousel motion.
  - show_arrows / show_dots: {Boolean} gallery chrome.
  - show_sku / show_description / show_dynamic_checkout: {Boolean} info panel.
  - details_open: {Boolean} render the details accordion already expanded.
  - shipping_title / shipping_content: {String} an extra accordion row.
  - care_title / care_content: {String} an extra accordion row.
  - info_width / sticky_bar_width: {Number} px.
  - show_sticky_bar: {Boolean} render the desktop purchase bar.
  - padding_top / padding_bottom: {Number} px.

  Usage:
  {% render 'product-hero-gallery', product: product, slides_desktop: 3 %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Every setting has a default here, so a caller can pass as few or as many as
    it exposes to merchants and the section still renders completely.
  endcomment
  assign phg_slides_desktop = slides_desktop | default: 3
  assign phg_slides_tablet = slides_tablet | default: 2
  assign phg_slides_mobile = slides_mobile | default: 1.15
  assign phg_gallery_ratio = gallery_ratio | default: '4 / 5'
  assign phg_gallery_max_height = gallery_max_height | default: 90
  assign phg_slide_gap = slide_gap | default: 4
  assign phg_autoplay_speed = autoplay_speed | default: 4000
  assign phg_transition_speed = transition_speed | default: 600
  assign phg_info_width = info_width | default: 640
  assign phg_bar_width = sticky_bar_width | default: 1720

  comment
    `default` treats false as empty, so booleans are read as "unset means on"
    (or off) rather than filtered.
  endcomment
  assign phg_full_bleed = true
  if full_bleed == false
    assign phg_full_bleed = false
  endif
  assign phg_autoplay = true
  if autoplay == false
    assign phg_autoplay = false
  endif
  assign phg_show_sticky_bar = true
  if show_sticky_bar == false
    assign phg_show_sticky_bar = false
  endif
  assign phg_show_sku = true
  if show_sku == false
    assign phg_show_sku = false
  endif
  assign phg_show_description = true
  if show_description == false
    assign phg_show_description = false
  endif
  assign phg_show_dynamic_checkout = true
  if show_dynamic_checkout == false
    assign phg_show_dynamic_checkout = false
  endif
  assign phg_show_arrows = false
  if show_arrows == true
    assign phg_show_arrows = true
  endif
  assign phg_show_dots = false
  if show_dots == true
    assign phg_show_dots = true
  endif
  comment
    Closed by default: the reference page leads with the purchase controls, and
    an open panel would push them down the page.
  endcomment
  assign phg_details_open = false
  if details_open == true
    assign phg_details_open = true
  endif

  comment
    The two standing rows next to the description. A row renders only when it
    has both a label and a body, so clearing either one removes it.
  endcomment
  assign phg_shipping_title = shipping_title | default: 'International Shipping Available'
  assign phg_care_title = care_title | default: 'Customer Care'

  assign phg_padding_top = padding_top | default: 0
  assign phg_padding_bottom = padding_bottom | default: 24
-%}

{{ 'slick.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'section-product-hero-gallery.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'component-accordion-item.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'component-price.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<script src="{{ 'product-info.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'product-form.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- comment -%}
  Slick 1.8.1 requires jQuery. Both are already vendored for the hero carousel,
  so this section adds no new dependency; identical script URLs are deduped by
  the browser.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'jquery.min.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'slick.min.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'product-hero-gallery.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'variant-media.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- if request.design_mode -%}
  <script src="{{ 'theme-editor.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product_form_id = 'product-form-' | append: section.id
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  comment
    Gallery source. Images only — this gallery is a photographic presentation,
    and a video or 3D model would need a player, which the reference design has
    no place for. Everything falls back to the product's featured image, then to
    a placeholder, so the layout never collapses.
  endcomment
  assign gallery_media = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'image'
  assign source_count = gallery_media.size

  comment
    Slick needs more slides than it shows before infinite mode can loop without
    a visible jump, and the design wants a full row whatever the catalogue has.
    Two full rows plus one is the smallest count that satisfies both, and never
    fewer than five so the loop stays smooth on the widest breakpoint.
  endcomment
  assign per_view = phg_slides_desktop | ceil
  assign minimum_slides = per_view | times: 2 | plus: 1
  if minimum_slides < 5
    assign minimum_slides = 5
  endif

  comment
    Repeat the real images until there are enough slides. Ceiling division:
    (minimum + count - 1) / count. The product's own media list is never
    mutated — this only controls how many times the loop below runs.
  endcomment
  assign repeat_count = 1
  if source_count > 0
    assign repeat_count = minimum_slides | plus: source_count | minus: 1 | divided_by: source_count
  endif
  if repeat_count < 1
    assign repeat_count = 1
  endif

  assign featured_media_id = variant.featured_media.id
-%}

{%- capture gallery_sizes -%}
  (min-width: 990px) {{ 100.0 | divided_by: phg_slides_desktop | round: 1 }}vw,
  (min-width: 750px) {{ 100.0 | divided_by: phg_slides_tablet | round: 1 }}vw,
  {{ 100.0 | divided_by: phg_slides_mobile | round: 1 }}vw
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- style -%}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
    /* Drives the pre-Slick fallback row; Slick sizes the slides itself once it
       initialises. */
    --phg-slides: {{ phg_slides_mobile }};
    --phg-slide-ratio: {{ phg_gallery_ratio }};
    --phg-slide-gap: {{ phg_slide_gap }}px;
    --phg-gallery-max-height: {{ phg_gallery_max_height }}svh;
    --phg-info-width: {{ phg_info_width }}px;
    --phg-bar-width: {{ phg_bar_width }}px;
    --phg-padding-top: {{ phg_padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    --phg-padding-bottom: {{ phg_padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
      --phg-slides: {{ phg_slides_tablet }};
      --phg-padding-top: {{ phg_padding_top }}px;
      --phg-padding-bottom: {{ phg_padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
      --phg-slides: {{ phg_slides_desktop }};
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<div class="phg{% if phg_full_bleed %} phg--full-bleed{% endif %}{% if phg_show_sticky_bar %} phg--has-bar{% endif %}">
  <product-component view-event-payload="{{ product | standard_event_data: 'view', context: 'page' | escape }}">
    <product-hero-gallery
      class="phg__stage"
      data-slides-desktop="{{ phg_slides_desktop }}"
      data-slides-tablet="{{ phg_slides_tablet }}"
      data-slides-mobile="{{ phg_slides_mobile }}"
      data-infinite="true"
      data-autoplay="{{ phg_autoplay }}"
      data-autoplay-speed="{{ phg_autoplay_speed }}"
      data-speed="{{ phg_transition_speed }}"
      data-arrows="{{ phg_show_arrows }}"
      data-dots="{{ phg_show_dots }}"
      data-repeated="{{ repeat_count }}"
      data-slide-label="{{ 'products.product.media.gallery_viewer' | t | escape }}"
      data-quantity-label="{{ 'products.product.quantity.label' | t | escape }}"
    >
      {%- comment -%} ------------------------------------------- Gallery {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="phg-gallery">
        <div class="phg-gallery__track" data-gallery-track>
          {%- if source_count > 0 -%}
            {%- assign slide_index = 0 -%}
            {%- for repeat in (1..repeat_count) -%}
              {%- for media in gallery_media -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign is_original = false
                  if repeat == 1
                    assign is_original = true
                  endif

                  comment
                    Only the first pass carries the variant flag, so the
                    gallery always jumps to a real image rather than one of
                    its repeats.
                  endcomment
                  assign is_variant_featured = false
                  if is_original and featured_media_id != blank and media.id == featured_media_id
                    assign is_variant_featured = true
                  endif

                  assign loading_attr = 'lazy'
                  if slide_index < per_view
                    assign loading_attr = 'eager'
                  endif
                -%}
                <div
                  class="phg-gallery__slide"
                  data-gallery-slide
                  data-gallery-index="{{ slide_index }}"
                  data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
                  {% if is_variant_featured %}
                    data-variant-featured="true"
                  {% endif %}
                  {% unless is_original %}
                    data-gallery-repeat="true"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  {% endunless %}
                >
                  {{
                    media.preview_image
                    | image_url: width: 1946
                    | image_tag:
                      loading: loading_attr,
                      fetchpriority: 'auto',
                      class: 'phg-gallery__image',
                      widths: '375, 550, 750, 1100, 1500, 1780, 2000',
                      sizes: gallery_sizes,
                      alt: media.alt
                  }}
                </div>
                {%- assign slide_index = slide_index | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              No media at all: keep the same slide box so the page's shape
              is unchanged, using the theme's own placeholder.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- for i in (1..minimum_slides) -%}
              <div class="phg-gallery__slide" data-gallery-slide data-gallery-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}">
                {{ 'product-apparel-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'phg-gallery__image phg-gallery__image--placeholder' }}
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if phg_show_arrows -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            class="phg-gallery__arrow phg-gallery__arrow--prev"
            data-gallery-prev
            aria-label="{{ 'general.slider.previous_slide' | t }}"
          >
            <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-arrow.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          </button>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="phg-gallery__arrow phg-gallery__arrow--next"
            data-gallery-next
            aria-label="{{ 'general.slider.next_slide' | t }}"
          >
            <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-arrow.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          </button>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if phg_show_dots -%}
          <div class="phg-gallery__dots" data-gallery-dots></div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <p class="visually-hidden" data-gallery-live aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} -------------------------------------- Product info {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="phg-info">
        <div class="phg-info__inner" data-phg-info>
          {%- comment -%}
            Everything the floating bar also carries lives in one box, so the
            desktop rule that stands it down is a single selector. It stays in
            the DOM and in the form: the bar's controls write to these inputs
            and its buttons click these buttons.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="phg-info__purchase">
          {%- if phg_show_sku -%}
            <p class="phg-info__sku" id="Sku-{{ section.id }}" role="status" data-phg-sku-source>
              <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.product.sku' | t }}:</span>
              {{ variant.sku }}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}

          <h1 class="phg-info__title">{{ product.title | escape }}</h1>

          <div class="phg-info__price" id="price-{{ section.id }}" role="status" data-phg-price-source>
            {%- render 'price', product: product, use_variant: true, show_badges: false, price_class: '' -%}
          </div>

          {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
            <variant-selects
              id="variant-selects-{{ section.id }}"
              class="phg-options"
              data-section="{{ section.id }}"
              data-product-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
              data-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
              data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
              data-currency-code="{{ cart.currency.iso_code }}"
              {% # theme-check-disable %}
              data-selected-price-amount="{{ variant.price | default: 0 | money_amount | escape }}"
              {% # theme-check-enable %}
            >
              {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
                {%- liquid
                  comment
                    Colour-named options render as circles using the shared
                    variant-picker-color resolver, so plain value names like
                    "Cream" resolve without merchant metafields. Any other
                    option still needs a swatch on every value to become
                    circles; otherwise it is drawn as labelled pills.
                  endcomment
                  assign option_name_down = option.name | downcase | strip
                  assign is_color_option = false
                  assign phg_color_names = 'color,colour,colors,colours,shade,tone' | split: ','
                  for phg_color_name in phg_color_names
                    if option_name_down == phg_color_name
                      assign is_color_option = true
                      break
                    endif
                  endfor

                  assign swatch_count = option.values | map: 'swatch' | compact | size
                  assign use_swatches = false
                  if is_color_option or swatch_count == option.values.size
                    assign use_swatches = true
                  endif
                -%}
                <fieldset
                  class="phg-options__group product-form__input"
                  data-phg-option-group
                  data-option-name="{{ option.name | escape }}"
                >
                  <legend class="phg-options__label">
                    <span class="phg-options__name">{{ option.name }}</span>
                    <span class="phg-options__divider" aria-hidden="true">|</span>
                    <span class="phg-options__value" data-selected-value>{{ option.selected_value }}</span>
                  </legend>

                  <div
                    class="phg-options__values{% if use_swatches %} phg-options__values--swatch{% endif %}"
                    data-phg-radio-group
                  >
                    {%- for value in option.values -%}
                      {%- liquid
                        assign input_id = 'PhgOption-' | append: section.id | append: '-' | append: option.position | append: '-' | append: forloop.index0
                        assign input_name = option.name | append: '-' | append: option.position
                        capture phg_swatch_css
                          render 'variant-picker-color', swatch: value.swatch, title: value
                        endcapture
                        assign phg_swatch_css = phg_swatch_css | strip
                      -%}
                      <input
                        type="radio"
                        class="phg-options__input{% unless value.available %} phg-options__input--unavailable{% endunless %}"
                        id="{{ input_id }}"
                        name="{{ input_name | escape }}"
                        value="{{ value | escape }}"
                        form="{{ product_form_id }}"
                        {% if value.selected %}
                          checked
                        {% endif %}
                        data-product-url="{{ value.product_url }}"
                        data-option-value-id="{{ value.id }}"
                        data-option-name="{{ option.name | escape }}"
                      >
                      <label
                        class="phg-options__swatch{% unless use_swatches %} phg-options__pill{% endunless %}{% if use_swatches and phg_swatch_css == blank %} phg-options__swatch--fallback{% endif %}"
                        for="{{ input_id }}"
                        {% if use_swatches and phg_swatch_css != blank %}
                          style="background: {{ phg_swatch_css }};"
                        {% endif %}
                      >
                        {%- if use_swatches -%}
                          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ value }}</span>
                        {%- else -%}
                          {{ value }}
                        {%- endif -%}
                        {%- unless value.available -%}
                          <span class="visually-hidden">
                            {{- 'products.product.variant_sold_out_or_unavailable' | t -}}
                          </span>
                        {%- endunless -%}
                      </label>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </div>
                </fieldset>
              {%- endfor -%}

              <script type="application/json" data-selected-variant>
                {{ variant | json }}
              </script>
            </variant-selects>
            {%- render 'variant-media-data',
              product: product,
              section: section,
              vm_media_list: gallery_media,
              vm_repeat_count: repeat_count
            -%}
          {%- endunless -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Custom stepper markup. The <quantity-input> element and the
            .quantity__* / Quantity-Form-* hooks stay because they are what
            enforces the shop's own quantity rules — minimums, increments
            and per-order maximums come back from the cart, and the theme
            reads and rewrites exactly these nodes when they change.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {% # theme-check-disable %}
          {%- assign cart_qty = cart | item_count_for_variant: variant.id -%}
          {% # theme-check-enable %}
          <div class="phg-quantity product-form__quantity" id="Quantity-Form-{{ section.id }}">
            <span class="visually-hidden" id="quantity-label-{{ section.id }}">
              {%- if cart_qty > 0 -%}
                {{- 'products.product.quantity.in_cart_aria_label' | t: quantity: cart_qty -}}
              {%- else -%}
                {{- 'products.product.quantity.label' | t -}}
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
            <label
              class="phg-quantity__label quantity__label"
              for="Quantity-{{ section.id }}"
              aria-labelledby="quantity-label-{{ section.id }}"
            >
              <span aria-hidden="true">{{ 'products.product.quantity.label' | t }}</span>
              <span class="quantity__rules-cart{% if cart_qty == 0 %} hidden{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true">
                {%- render 'loading-spinner' -%}
                <span>({{ 'products.product.quantity.in_cart_html' | t: quantity: cart_qty }})</span>
              </span>
            </label>
            <quantity-input class="phg-quantity__control">
              <button
                class="phg-quantity__button quantity__button"
                name="minus"
                type="button"
              >
                <span class="visually-hidden">
                  {{- 'products.product.quantity.decrease' | t: product: product.title | escape -}}
                </span>
                <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-minus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
              </button>
              <input
                class="phg-quantity__input quantity__input"
                type="number"
                name="quantity"
                id="Quantity-{{ section.id }}"
                data-cart-quantity="{{ cart_qty }}"
                data-min="{{ variant.quantity_rule.min }}"
                min="{{ variant.quantity_rule.min }}"
                {% if variant.quantity_rule.max != null %}
                  data-max="{{ variant.quantity_rule.max }}"
                  max="{{ variant.quantity_rule.max }}"
                {% endif %}
                step="{{ variant.quantity_rule.increment }}"
                value="{{ variant.quantity_rule.min }}"
                form="{{ product_form_id }}"
              >
              <button
                class="phg-quantity__button quantity__button"
                name="plus"
                type="button"
              >
                <span class="visually-hidden">
                  {{- 'products.product.quantity.increase' | t: product: product.title | escape -}}
                </span>
                <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-plus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
              </button>
            </quantity-input>
            <div class="phg-quantity__rules quantity__rules" id="Quantity-Rules-{{ section.id }}"></div>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            <product-form> wraps the buy buttons and nothing else, exactly as it
            does in Dawn: it treats the first .loading__spinner and the first
            [type=submit] inside itself as the ones belonging to Add to cart,
            and the quantity block above has a spinner of its own.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <product-form class="phg__form-wrapper" data-hide-errors="false" data-section-id="{{ section.id }}">
            <div class="phg__form-error" role="alert" hidden>
              <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
              <span class="product-form__error-message"></span>
            </div>

            {%- form 'product',
              product,
              id: product_form_id,
              class: 'phg__form',
              novalidate: 'novalidate',
              data-type: 'add-to-cart-form'
            -%}
              <input
                type="hidden"
                name="id"
                value="{{ variant.id }}"
                {% if variant.available == false or variant == null %}
                  disabled
                {% endif %}
                class="product-variant-id"
              >

              <div class="phg-actions">
                <button
                  id="ProductSubmitButton-{{ section.id }}"
                  type="submit"
                  name="add"
                  class="phg-button phg-button--secondary"
                  data-phg-submit
                  {% if variant.available == false or variant == null %}
                    disabled
                  {% endif %}
                >
                  <span class="phg-button__label">
                    {%- if variant == null -%}
                      {{ 'products.product.unavailable' | t }}
                    {%- elsif variant.available == false -%}
                      {{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                  {%- render 'loading-spinner' -%}
                </button>

                {%- if phg_show_dynamic_checkout -%}
                  <div class="phg-actions__dynamic" data-phg-dynamic-checkout>
                    {{ form | payment_button }}
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endform -%}
          </product-form>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            The details sit behind an accordion rather than running down the
            page: on desktop the purchase controls are what the panel is for,
            and a long description pushed everything else out of view.
            snippets/accordion-item.liquid is a plain <details> row, so it
            needs no script and stays keyboard operable.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign details_group = 'phg-details-' | append: section.id
            assign details_id = 'PhgDetails-' | append: section.id
            assign shipping_id = 'PhgShipping-' | append: section.id
            assign care_id = 'PhgCare-' | append: section.id
            assign details_title = 'products.product.description' | t

            assign description_row = ''
            if phg_show_description
              assign description_row = product.description
            endif

            comment
              The wrapper draws the rules between rows, so it is only worth
              rendering when at least one row has both a label and a body.
            endcomment
            assign has_details = false
            if description_row != blank
              assign has_details = true
            endif
            if phg_shipping_title != blank and shipping_content != blank
              assign has_details = true
            endif
            if phg_care_title != blank and care_content != blank
              assign has_details = true
            endif
          -%}
          {%- if has_details -%}
          <div class="accordion phg-accordion">
            {%- render 'accordion-item',
              id: details_id,
              group: details_group,
              title: details_title,
              content: description_row,
              open: phg_details_open
            -%}
            {%- render 'accordion-item',
              id: shipping_id,
              group: details_group,
              title: phg_shipping_title,
              content: shipping_content
            -%}
            {%- render 'accordion-item',
              id: care_id,
              group: details_group,
              title: phg_care_title,
              content: care_content
            -%}
          </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ---------------------------------- Sticky purchase bar {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if phg_show_sticky_bar -%}
        <span class="phg-bar__sentinel" data-gallery-sentinel aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="phg-bar" data-gallery-bar>
          <div class="phg-bar__inner">
            <div class="phg-bar__summary">
              <div class="phg-bar__thumb">
                {%- if source_count > 0 -%}
                  <img
                    src="{{ gallery_media.first.preview_image | image_url: width: 200 }}"
                    srcset="
                      {{ gallery_media.first.preview_image | image_url: width: 100 }} 100w,
                      {{ gallery_media.first.preview_image | image_url: width: 200 }} 200w
                    "
                    sizes="64px"
                    width="64"
                    height="64"
                    loading="lazy"
                    alt=""
                    class="phg-bar__thumb-image"
                    data-phg-bar-thumb
                  >
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
              <div class="phg-bar__text">
                {%- if phg_show_sku -%}
                  <p class="phg-bar__sku" data-phg-bar-sku>{{ variant.sku }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
                <p class="phg-bar__title">{{ product.title | escape }}</p>
                <div class="phg-bar__price" data-phg-bar-price>
                  {%- render 'price', product: product, use_variant: true, show_badges: false, price_class: '' -%}
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              The bar's Colour and Quantity controls are built by
              product-hero-gallery.js from the real inputs above and write
              straight back to them, so there is no second copy of the
              selection to drift out of step. These slots stay empty — and
              the bar stays valid — if the script never runs.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="phg-bar__controls" data-phg-bar-controls></div>

            <div class="phg-bar__actions">
              <button type="button" class="phg-button phg-button--secondary phg-bar__add" data-phg-bar-add>
                <span class="phg-button__label">{{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}</span>
              </button>
              {%- comment -%}
                Shopify owns the dynamic checkout button, including its
                wording in each language, so the bar's twin takes its label
                from the real button rather than inventing one. It stays
                hidden until that button exists.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if phg_show_dynamic_checkout -%}
                <button type="button" class="phg-button phg-button--primary phg-bar__buy" data-phg-bar-buy hidden>
                  <span class="phg-button__label"></span>
                </button>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          The bar is sticky, so it leaves with the section. This widget takes
          over from there: a compact card in the corner that keeps the product
          and its Add to cart within reach for the rest of the page.

          It mirrors the same sources the bar does and clicks the same button,
          so it is a third view of one state rather than another copy of it.
          Hidden until product-hero-gallery.js sees the section leave the
          viewport, and dismissible.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <aside
          class="phg-mini"
          data-phg-mini
          aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}"
        >
          <div class="phg-mini__thumb">
            {%- if source_count > 0 -%}
              <img
                src="{{ gallery_media.first.preview_image | image_url: width: 200 }}"
                srcset="
                  {{ gallery_media.first.preview_image | image_url: width: 120 }} 120w,
                  {{ gallery_media.first.preview_image | image_url: width: 240 }} 240w
                "
                sizes="60px"
                width="60"
                height="60"
                loading="lazy"
                alt=""
                class="phg-mini__thumb-image"
                data-phg-mini-thumb
              >
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>

          <div class="phg-mini__text">
            <p class="phg-mini__title">{{ product.title | escape }}</p>
            {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
              <p class="phg-mini__variant" data-phg-mini-variant>{{ variant.title }}</p>
            {%- endunless -%}
            <div class="phg-mini__price" data-phg-mini-price>
              {%- render 'price', product: product, use_variant: true, show_badges: false, price_class: '' -%}
            </div>
          </div>

          <button
            type="button"
            class="phg-mini__close"
            data-phg-mini-close
            aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}"
          >
            <span class="svg-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
              {{- 'icon-close.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            </span>
          </button>

          <button
            type="button"
            class="phg-mini__add"
            data-phg-mini-add
            aria-label="{{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}"
          >
            <span class="svg-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
              {{- 'icon-bag.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            </span>
          </button>
        </aside>
      {%- endif -%}
    </product-hero-gallery>
  </product-component>
</div>
